<title>POLAND: POLISH GDYNIA PORT CARGO TRANSFER UP 18 PCT IN H1.</title>
<headline>POLISH GDYNIA PORT CARGO TRANSFER UP 18 PCT IN H1.</headline>
<dateline>GDANSK, Poland 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo transfer in the</p>
<p>Polish port of Gdynia rose 18.3 percent in the first half of</p>
<p>this year against the same period of last year to 4.68 million</p>
<p>tonnes, the port's management said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p> (IN MLN T)		 H1 1997   H1 1996  pct difference</p>
<p> TOTAL			  4.68     3.95	18.3</p>
<p> COAL			   1.03     0.81	27.5</p>
<p> IRON ORE		     0.03     0.05     -38.9</p>
<p> MASS PRODUCTS		0.39     0.39	-2.3</p>
<p> GRAIN			  0.64     0.70	-9.7</p>
<p> WOOD			   0.001    0.002    -50.0</p>
<p> FUEL			   0.31     0.12     162.9</p>
<p> SMALL BULK		   2.28     1.87	21.9</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
